It is possible.  If you have 2MB or more, use Os/2 1.3 and
the os/2 version of nethack.  (Perhaps it works with less memory too, but
the documentation for os/2 says it needs 2MB.)
You don't need to install os/2 if you don't want to, it can boot from
a diskette.  Using os/2 will allow nethack to use all memory, with
no 640k barrier.  If this isn't enough, you may get some swapping.

You may also try msdos v. 5.  Load msdos and ansi.sys into high memory, 
use the rest of high memory as a disk cache.  With a large enough disk cache,
most swapping will be to the cache rather than the disk, so it won't be
too slow.  Don't load any memory-resident program or device driver that
you don't need for nethack.
